ical work: for works published 2020–2022, the median FWCI is 0.17–0.19. In every year, half of the works received at most 19% of the citations expected for similar works worldwide (FWCI 1 = world average).","Above the world average: 8%–9% of the works per year have an FWCI above 1, most in 2022 (9%).","Not cited: on average 38% of these works have FWCI 0, meaning no citations within their four-year window. That is why many boxes start at 0.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 3 of 3 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2020: mean 0.31, median 0.17, top work 1.61. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Still counting: works from 2023–2026 have not completed their four-year citation window, so their values will rise. Do not compare them with older years yet."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2020–2023 have a median of 0–2.5 citations each; the highest median (2.5) is in 2020.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2020 have at least 8.3 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Not yet cited: more than half of the works published 2023–2026 have no citations so far. This is expected for recent works and is not a sign of low quality.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 4 of 4 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2020: mean 4.7, median 2.5, top work 47. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Recent years: works from 2024–2026 have had less than three years to be cited, so their values will rise."]}}}